{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"═══ RESULT: the hoist is implemented and precision is preserved 12/12, but the measured token\noutcome is a REGRESSION of +936 (+5.8%), because the hoisted prefix lands at 846 tokens against a\nmeasured 1024 floor. Reported as a regression, not dressed up. ═══\n\n**BEFORE / AFTER, real `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` calls, same query ticket, same six candidate\ndigests, same order, 12 calls each.** BEFORE is the shipped `judge.py` reverted via `git stash`, so\nthe two runs differ only in this change.\n\n                                        BEFORE     AFTER\n    stable system prefix (count_tokens)     423       846      floor 1024\n    distinct system prompts per batch         1         1\n    input_tokens (total)                 16,040    16,976      +936  (+5.8%)\n    cache_read_tokens                         0         0\n    cache_write_tokens                        0         0\n    surfaced findings                        []        []\n\n`cache_write_tokens` did not rise above one prefix write — it stayed at zero, so the \"N writes\ninstead of 1\" failure mode did not occur. Nothing cached at all: 846 < 1024. The +936 is the\norientation paragraph that reconciles the base prompt's \"you are given TWO digests\" framing with\nthe split, carried on all 12 calls.\n\n**THE FLOOR IS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED — and it is 1024, not the 4096 in `capabilities.py:330`.**\nThrough the real judge request path: an 875-token system prefix gave write 0 / read 0; a\n1250-token one gave write 1243 then read 1243 on the next call. Against the bare API the same\nboundary appears between 922 (nothing) and 1042 (write 1035, then read 1035). So the caching\nmachinery works on this exact path and the prefix is simply too small. `count_tokens` over the base\nprompt (423) plus each of seven real digests (306-453) gives 728-875 — short of 1024 by 149-296\ntokens for every ticket measured.\n\n**PRECISION PRESERVED: relations identical on 12 of 12 ordered pairs.**\n\n    049e#q_first    unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.92 -> 0.95\n    049e#q_second   unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.95 -> 0.95\n    061c#q_first    related_distinct -> related_distinct   conf 0.62 -> 0.62\n    061c#q_second   related_distinct -> related_distinct   conf 0.35 -> 0.62\n    06e0#q_first    unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.85 -> 0.85\n    06e0#q_second   unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.85 -> 0.85\n    79d5#q_first    unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.92 -> 0.92\n    79d5#q_second   unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.95 -> 0.85\n    cc77#q_first    unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.92 -> 0.85\n    cc77#q_second   unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.92 -> 0.85\n    dbf9#q_first    unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.95 -> 0.95\n    dbf9#q_second   unrelated        -> unrelated          conf 0.95 -> 0.85\n\nNo relation changed and no finding changed. Confidences move within sampling variance (the largest\nmove, 0.35 -> 0.62 on 061c#q_second, is on a `related_distinct` verdict that is not surfaceable\neither way, and its `shared_artifact` went from `prompts.resolve_prompt_cached` to the broader\n`prompt caching`). The pointer-for-inline-digest substitution did not degrade the judge on this\ncorpus.\n\n**MUTATION EVIDENCE, BOTH DIRECTIONS.** Restored code: 20 passed, exit 0. Each mutation applied\nalone, then reverted:\n\n    M1  judge() stops passing shared_side          -> FAILS test_shared_query_digest_lives_only_in_the_system_prompt,\n                                                              test_hoisted_reference_keeps_the_ordered_pair_slots\n    M2  system prompt no longer carries the digest -> FAILS test_shared_query_digest_lives_only_in_the_system_prompt\n    M3  ordering-2 slot wrong (ref in FIRST twice) -> FAILS both hoist tests\n    M4  default path also hoists                   -> FAILS test_judge_one_default_shape_is_unchanged (+ the hoist test)\n    M5  missing-corpus candidate judged anyway     -> FAILS test_missing_corpus_digest_makes_no_call\n\nEvery new test dies on at least one mutation and passes on the restored tree; no mutation survived.\n\n**GATES, by exit code:** `make lint` 0, `make typecheck` 0,\n`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 6 --dist worksteal` 0 (8968 passed, 39 skipped).\n\n**FOLLOW-UP FILED:** `c403-cc3a-2c6d-4b9d` (ore-wretched-nene), linked `discovered_from` this\nticket — batch candidates per call to close the 149-296 token gap, carrying these numbers and the\nprecision-parity requirement.\n\n**NOT CHANGED, deliberately:** `capabilities.py`'s `CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS = 4096` is correct for\nthe Opus-class model it documents; making it model-aware is separate work. One consequence worth\nrecording: because that constant also gates `warn_if_cache_ineffective`, a silent caching failure at\nthis sub-4096 call site would never warn."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785710971531664001,"uuid":"baa582fc-1722-4032-b7b7-269ce89dec72"}